{
  "id": "kantu_charazani",
  "name": "K'antu (Charazani panpipe-and-drum troupes)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Panpipe-and-drum troupe music of the Kallawaya region around Charazani in Bautista Saavedra province, in the highlands of La Paz department, Bolivia, part of the Andean cosmovision of the Kallawaya that UNESCO recognises as Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity. Men play k'antu panpipes split into two complementary rows, ira and arka, in several sizes doubling the melody at parallel intervals, many of them beating a large drum (wankara) as they play, while a triangle rings above. The siku card stands in for the k'antu panpipes and the membrane-drum card for the wankara.",
  "recipe": "classic modern k'antu, carnival Processional, andean branch. andean tradition paired rows interlocking siku panpipes, membrane drum pulse resonant acoustic membrane drum, concert triangle. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
